{"agent":"bg93","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_arm_parent_death_signal` is a `preexec_fn` that calls `ctypes.CDLL(\"libc.so.6\")` after fork. CPython documents that `preexec_fn` is not thread-safe: if any other thread holds the allocator or dynamic-linker lock at the moment `_spawn` forks (pytest-cov, timeout plugins, logging threads), the child blocks forever inside `dlopen`/`prctl` and the parent blocks in `Popen` waiting for an exec that never happens. Every caller of `_spawn`, not only the new test, hangs on that input; a raw `prctl` syscall without `dlopen` in the child would not.","digest":"c999cf8ee9b017f0","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Arming `PR_SET_PDEATHSIG` without the `getppid()==1` check leaves the orphan the comment claims is impossible. If the worker is killed after `fork` returns in the parent and before `preexec_fn` runs, the child is already reparented to init; `prctl` then succeeds with no pending signal, and the daemon stays up forever. The new test never hits that window: it only `kill()`s the spawner after `_pid_under` sees a pidfile, which is after exec, so it can pass while that start-up race still reproduces B2d2c474d47.","digest":"a3b43282cd9e4bb3","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":4445,"diff_sha":"365e1f58fedc5591b1a76d953de1893407c1c5750dcdbe7704b384825e37ea3e","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B2d2c474d47","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":325.5,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"646b4ea5ae22b356","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B2d2c474d47.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T194411Z-120d9d60.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794167051.1185095,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}],"review_id":"4996804c3051","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"e89977b382ea90f835493a0d458c21200073c70a","reviewed_paths":{"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py":"100644 88f88819cdcc6fc01689cfbd82fd40c12ae77719"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45","tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45"],"tree_sha":"e89977b382ea+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e26ac791b36240d809323293b","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":157003,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B2d2c474d47","ts":"2026-11-08T19:49:36.895013Z"}
{"agent":"bg93","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_arm_parent_death_signal` is a `preexec_fn` that calls `ctypes.CDLL(\"libc.so.6\")` after fork. CPython documents that `preexec_fn` is not thread-safe: if any other thread holds the allocator or dynamic-linker lock at the moment `_spawn` forks (pytest-cov, timeout plugins, logging threads), the child blocks forever inside `dlopen`/`prctl` and the parent blocks in `Popen` waiting for an exec that never happens. Every caller of `_spawn`, not only the new test, hangs on that input; a raw `prctl` syscall without `dlopen` in the child would not.","digest":"c999cf8ee9b017f0","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Arming `PR_SET_PDEATHSIG` without the `getppid()==1` check leaves the orphan the comment claims is impossible. If the worker is killed after `fork` returns in the parent and before `preexec_fn` runs, the child is already reparented to init; `prctl` then succeeds with no pending signal, and the daemon stays up forever. The new test never hits that window: it only `kill()`s the spawner after `_pid_under` sees a pidfile, which is after exec, so it can pass while that start-up race still reproduces B2d2c474d47.","digest":"a3b43282cd9e4bb3","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":4445,"diff_sha":"365e1f58fedc5591b1a76d953de1893407c1c5750dcdbe7704b384825e37ea3e","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B2d2c474d47","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":325.5,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"646b4ea5ae22b356","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B2d2c474d47.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T194411Z-120d9d60.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794167051.1185095,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}],"review_id":"4996804c3051","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"e89977b382ea90f835493a0d458c21200073c70a","reviewed_paths":{"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py":"100644 88f88819cdcc6fc01689cfbd82fd40c12ae77719"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45","tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:45"],"tree_sha":"e89977b382ea+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e222008e667a5aa6efc4559c0","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":157004,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B2d2c474d47","ts":"2026-11-08T19:49:38.433183Z"}
