{"agent":"bg93","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The earlier preexec_fn deadlock still stands. Loading `libc.so.6` at import only removes `dlopen` from the child; `_arm_parent_death_signal` is still a Python `preexec_fn`, and CPython runs it after `fork` in a child that inherits lock ownership. If any other thread holds the GIL (or the allocator) when `_spawn` forks — pytest-cov, timeout plugins, logging — the child blocks forever inside the `prctl`/`getppid` bytecode and the parent blocks in `Popen` waiting for an exec that never happens. Every `_spawn` caller hangs on that input, not only the new test.","digest":"b07b7f3bce67f7cf","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:40","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:40"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `getppid() == 1` guard does not close the fork-to-prctl window the comment claims. If the worker is killed after `fork` returns in the parent and before `preexec_fn` runs, the child is already reparented. Under a child subreaper (`PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER`, typical of `systemd --user` and some container/pytest supervisors) the new parent is not pid 1, so the check does not `_exit`, `prctl` arms `PR_SET_PDEATHSIG` against a parent that is already dead, and no signal is pending. The daemon then execs and stays up forever — the same orphan as B2d2c474d47. The new test never hits that window: it `kill()`s the spawner only after `_pid_under` sees a pidfile, which is after exec, so it passes even if this check is deleted or wrong.","digest":"0f270bc8a63a73e8","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:46","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:46"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":4751,"diff_sha":"51cacba4eecc4e7350142cd16f3e73cac8fc000d0a2714c9c54bde10bbbb59d3","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B2d2c474d47","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":81.3,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"6bde7b6d5db41b17","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B2d2c474d47.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T195103Z-3206817c.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794167463.1918335,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}],"review_id":"d2e39f2360f1","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"0abfeee33b0ce16d49bd2e795c8b38794f255ab8","reviewed_paths":{"tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py":"100644 9f80344a60fbbb242ca35d1b1f21d7ecb9ceb275"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["xai"],"round":2,"rounds":2,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:40","tests/test_isolation_roborev_daemon.py:46"],"tree_sha":"0abfeee33b0c+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e048d56819012adb83c1e98fb","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":157015,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B2d2c474d47","ts":"2026-11-08T19:52:24.752695Z"}
